 "editorial": {
  "cups": {
   "2024.l.68899.t.12": "Never left the top three. Won the title without scoring points.",
   "2024.l.68899.t.7": "Owned the best player in fantasy and still lost the final.",
   "2024.l.68899.t.1": "Lost a semi in the one category he never loses.",
   "2024.l.68899.t.11": "No. 2 seed, luckiest record, beaten on free throws by three thousandths."
  },
  "bubble": {
   "headline": "Parth Rises From 12th, Arnav Falls Off a Cliff",
   "sub": "Who came from nowhere, and who coughed it up down the stretch.",
   "cards": [
    {
     "team": "2024.l.68899.t.7",
     "tag": "Came from nowhere",
     "body": "Dead last for three straight weeks and still 7th with six weeks to go. Then Parth ripped off a run to the 3 seed and rode the waiver wire all the way to the final."
    },
    {
     "team": "2024.l.68899.t.3",
     "tag": "Snuck in",
     "body": "In the top six for 10 weeks, out for 8, never higher than 4th. Finished as the 5 seed: never comfortable, never out, never worth fearing."
    },
    {
     "team": "2024.l.68899.t.9",
     "tag": "Crashed out",
     "body": "Sat 4th with six weeks to play. Then 5th, 7th, 8th, 8th. Arnav missed the playoffs entirely, then won the whole thing the next year. Rehab works."
    },
    {
     "team": "2024.l.68899.t.5",
     "tag": "Too little, too late",
     "body": "Won the final week 9-2 and still finished 7th, after six straight weeks parked in 8th. The comeback started about a month too late."
    }
   ]
  },
  "spicy": {
   "20-7-11": {
    "headline": "Parth Rents the Waiver Wire and Steals a Semi",
    "body": [
     "On paper, this was Keshav's week. Assists were Suggs's best category all year, and Parth rarely won them. So Parth went shopping: Tre Jones, gone from his roster by season's end, dished 28 assists, and Quentin Grimes, a pickup, added 25 more with 125 points and 18 threes. Assists went to Parth by eight.",
     "Threes, another Parth weakness, fell the same way. Grimes and Malik Beasley, a since-dropped rental, combined for 35 of Parth's 91.",
     "Then the comedy. Parth cut Keldon Johnson mid-week, Keshav scooped him up, and Keldon chipped in 3 blocks and 3 steals against his old team. It didn't matter. Free throws decided it, .816 to .813. Three thousandths, and Keshav went home."
    ]
   },
   "20-1-12": {
    "headline": "White Mambas Win a Semi in Their Worst Category",
    "body": [
     "White Mambas lost the points category 14 times in 18 regular-season weeks. theInfamous won it 14 times. So naturally, Vishal won points by 150 in the semifinal.",
     "Anthony Edwards dropped 84, Austin Reaves 77, and Fred VanVleet hit 14 threes. White Mambas buried theInfamous from deep, 105 threes to 66.",
     "John J fought back where he lives: offensive boards by 41, with \u015eeng\u00fcn grabbing 47 rebounds and Josh Hart 36. Steals and blocks finished dead even. Assists went to John J by three. It still came up one category short, and the one that killed him was the one he never loses."
    ]
   }
  },
  "awards": {
   "Horseshoe award": "Sat at No. 1 for most of the season on a record the numbers never backed up. The bill came in the semifinal: three thousandths of a free throw.",
   "Robbed": "Numbers good enough for 6th on paper, finished 8th. Owned Jayson Tatum and Dyson Daniels, two top-10 fantasy players, and still watched the playoffs from the couch.",
   "Waiver wire addict": "Churned the wire harder than anyone and won the title doing it. Three pickups, De'Andre Hunter, Brandin Podziemski and Donte DiVincenzo, combined for 151 points in the semifinal."
  }
 },
